{
  "_read": "Rules of wow_abilities.py: how a WoW mob's abilities become BG3 ones. No game data here, only names of spells on both sides and our choices. A rung is [min mob level, BG3 spell, options]; the highest rung at or below the mob's level applies, and below the first rung the mob does not get it. Options: rider = [status, turns, save ability or null] added to a hit; cond = a BG3 condition; dmg = true takes the damage from WoW's record through the fair dice; every = turn | recharge | fight overrides the cooldown; doubt = why this is unproven.",

  "power": {
    "_read": "wow_abilities.py reads these. level_cap: a member's BG3 level at WoW 60, as Scaling.lua. hero_hp: a member's BG3 HP by effective level (Scaling.lua M.MEMBER_HP), wow_hp: a WoW hero's HP by level; their ratio scales WoW damage. turn_share: what a spell that can fire every turn may do, as a share of a member's HP (the normal mob's hit of the balance research); every_cap, rank_cap and area_cap multiply it. hard_floor: lowest WoW level for each hard control, below it the soft version (hard_soft). abilities_low: most abilities at WoW 5 or below. off_spells: never given.",
